WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.480 --> 00:00:03.280
Spider-Man and Venom have long&nbsp;
been the best of archenemies,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:03.280 --> 00:00:07.680
but that complicated relationship hasn't quite&nbsp;
made it onto the big screen. The comics feature&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:07.680 --> 00:00:12.560
a true love-hate relationship with highs, lows,&nbsp;
and occasional team-ups to stop alien serial&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:12.560 --> 00:00:16.320
killers. This is the history of Venom's&nbsp;
relationship with Spider-Man explained.

00:00:17.040 --> 00:00:21.760
The Venom symbiote was first introduced in&nbsp;
1984 as part of the line-wide Marvel Comics&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:21.760 --> 00:00:25.920
crossover—or, as some might call it, the glorified&nbsp;
Mattel commercial— known as "Secret Wars."

00:00:25.920 --> 00:00:29.280
The storyline sees numerous heroes&nbsp;
and villains from the Marvel Universe&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:29.280 --> 00:00:33.520
kidnapped into space by a godlike alien&nbsp;
entity called the Beyonder, who deposits&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:33.520 --> 00:00:36.960
them on a planet he dubs "Battleworld"&nbsp;
and demands they fight one another.

00:00:36.960 --> 00:00:41.200
In the eighth issue, Spider-Man, needing a new&nbsp;
costume, is directed toward an alien machine that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:41.200 --> 00:00:45.760
can build him one. Of course, he picks the wrong&nbsp;
machine, and is introduced to a small black ball&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:45.760 --> 00:00:50.640
of unknown substance and origins — which quickly&nbsp;
covers his body and takes the form of a costume,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:50.640 --> 00:00:53.840
giving Spider-Man a new look for the&nbsp;
first time in the character's history&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:53.840 --> 00:00:57.840
(and, presumably, giving Mattel another&nbsp;
reason to make new Spider-Man toys).

00:00:58.400 --> 00:01:02.480
Technically, Spider-Man's black suit predates&nbsp;
"Secret Wars" by more than six months.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:02.480 --> 00:01:08.880
Spider-Man mysteriously vanishes from Earth at the&nbsp;
end of "Amazing Spider-Man" #251 in April 1984,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:08.880 --> 00:01:12.000
but returns at the start of the very&nbsp;
next issue wearing the black costume,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:15.760
with the entirety of "Secret Wars" having&nbsp;
occurred between the two issues. For the rest&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:15.760 --> 00:01:20.240
of the year, the events of "Secret Wars" unfold&nbsp;
retroactively in the pages of the crossover book,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:20.240 --> 00:01:23.920
while Spider-Man, wearing the black suit,&nbsp;
continued to do his usual stuff in his own&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:23.920 --> 00:01:28.320
comic. He occasionally considered how weird it was&nbsp;
that his new suit responded to his every thought,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:28.320 --> 00:01:31.840
but he didn't have time to worry about&nbsp;
it. Of course, he might have made time if&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:31.840 --> 00:01:36.000
he knew what the readers knew: that the suit&nbsp;
had started enveloping Peter while he slept,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:36.000 --> 00:01:39.680
dragging him around New York to fight&nbsp;
crime as Spider-Man without his knowledge.

00:01:39.680 --> 00:01:42.800
Eventually — after realizing the suit&nbsp;
had powers he didn't even know about,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:42.800 --> 00:01:47.120
and after it had displayed increasing reluctance&nbsp;
to leave his body — Spider-Man finally took it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:47.120 --> 00:01:51.920
to be examined by Reed Richards of the Fantastic&nbsp;
Four, who discovered the costume's true nature.

00:01:52.720 --> 00:01:56.480
Even for Spider-Man, it's not every day a&nbsp;
super-scientist tells you that the costume&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:56.480 --> 00:02:00.880
you've been wearing is not only a sentient alien,&nbsp;
but a sentient alien that is trying to permanently&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:00.880 --> 00:02:05.200
bond with you. Spider-Man's repulsed reaction is&nbsp;
perfectly understandable from a human point of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:05.200 --> 00:02:09.840
view. For the symbiote, however, it was rejection,&nbsp;
and rejection led to bitterness and hatred.

00:02:09.840 --> 00:02:13.760
Spider-Man managed to free himself from the&nbsp;
symbiote with the help of the Fantastic Four,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:13.760 --> 00:02:18.640
who used its weaknesses against sound and fire to&nbsp;
trap it in a containment unit for future study.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:18.640 --> 00:02:22.720
Eventually, it escaped, and managed to trick&nbsp;
Spider-Man into putting it back on by disguising&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:22.720 --> 00:02:26.880
itself as his more traditional blue-and-red&nbsp;
costume. It then attempted to forcibly bond&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:26.880 --> 00:02:30.800
with him, an effort that Peter was only able&nbsp;
to thwart by standing directly beside a set of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:30.800 --> 00:02:35.280
massive church bells, exposing both the symbiote&nbsp;
and himself to their ear-shattering resonance.

00:02:35.280 --> 00:02:39.040
The sound forced the symbiote to relinquish&nbsp;
its hold on its unwilling host. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:39.040 --> 00:02:42.800
despite Peter's rejection, the symbiote&nbsp;
saved his life by dragging his body away&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:42.800 --> 00:02:46.000
from the painfully loud noise,&nbsp;
foreshadowing the troubled future&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:46.000 --> 00:02:49.840
of their relationship — even at this early&nbsp;
stage, there was love mixed in with the hate.

00:02:50.720 --> 00:02:54.400
It would be three years before the symbiote&nbsp;
was seen again, but when it came back,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:54.400 --> 00:02:59.760
it came back quite literally with a vengeance.&nbsp;
The final page of "Amazing Spider-Man" #299,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:59.760 --> 00:03:04.160
published in April 1988, introduced the&nbsp;
character now popularly known as Venom,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:04.160 --> 00:03:07.920
though he didn't have knives for teeth&nbsp;
or the long, slavering tongue quite yet.

00:03:07.920 --> 00:03:11.760
"We are Venom."

00:03:11.760 --> 00:03:15.920
After being separated from Spider-Man in the&nbsp;
church, the symbiote had found a new host — Eddie&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:15.920 --> 00:03:20.400
Brock, a former journalist whose life and career&nbsp;
had been ruined, in his mind, by Spider-Man.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:20.400 --> 00:03:24.880
Preparing to commit suicide, the Catholic Brock&nbsp;
went to a church to pray for forgiveness. Instead,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:24.880 --> 00:03:28.960
he found the symbiote, which bonded to him — not&nbsp;
just physically, but emotionally, through their&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:28.960 --> 00:03:33.440
mutual hatred of Spider-Man. Naming themselves&nbsp;
Venom, Brock and the symbiote instantly became&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:33.440 --> 00:03:38.160
the webslinger's deadliest foe. Not only did they&nbsp;
not set off Peter's early warning spider-sense,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:38.160 --> 00:03:41.280
but they knew his true identity, and&nbsp;
were able to threaten his loved ones.

00:03:41.280 --> 00:03:45.840
While Spider-Man was never able to defeat Venom&nbsp;
in direct combat, he survived the late '80s and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:45.840 --> 00:03:51.040
early '90s largely due to trickery. In their first&nbsp;
meeting in "Amazing Spider-Man" #300, Peter uses&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:51.040 --> 00:03:55.920
his knowledge of how the symbiote works to defeat&nbsp;
Venom, while in "Amazing Spider-Man" #317, he&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:55.920 --> 00:04:00.560
pretends to take the symbiote back, revealing that&nbsp;
the alien still secretly wants to be with Peter,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:00.560 --> 00:04:04.960
not Brock — and the symbiote's attempt to break&nbsp;
its bond with Brock knocks them both unconscious.

00:04:05.760 --> 00:04:10.000
Venom's next two major appearances set up a&nbsp;
major shift in his relationship with Spider-Man,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:10.000 --> 00:04:14.560
which would see them reluctantly team up in the&nbsp;
face of a greater danger. "Amazing Spider-Man"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:14.560 --> 00:04:18.800
#333 features the apparent death of the&nbsp;
Venom symbiote at the cancerous hands of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:18.800 --> 00:04:22.640
the villain Styx. Depowered, Eddie Brock&nbsp;
is imprisoned for his crimes and placed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:22.640 --> 00:04:26.960
in a cell with a serial killer named Cletus&nbsp;
Kasady. The symbiote, however, isn't dead,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:26.960 --> 00:04:31.040
and it soon seeks Eddie out and breaks him&nbsp;
free. They continue to menace Spider-Man,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:31.040 --> 00:04:35.040
this time fighting him on a deserted island.&nbsp;
Peter tricks Venom for a third time by faking&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:35.040 --> 00:04:38.640
his own death, escaping the island while&nbsp;
Brock and the symbiote relax on the beach,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:38.640 --> 00:04:41.680
content in the knowledge that their&nbsp;
quest for revenge is complete.

00:04:41.680 --> 00:04:45.760
Venom might have lived out the rest of his days&nbsp;
on that island in peace, if not for the spawn&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:45.760 --> 00:04:50.160
the symbiote had left behind in Eddie's cell.&nbsp;
This second symbiote would bond with Kasady,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:50.160 --> 00:04:54.720
transforming him into the murderous villain known&nbsp;
as Carnage. For all Venom's hatred of Spider-Man,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:54.720 --> 00:04:58.240
he’s always had a code of honor that usually&nbsp;
prevents him from killing the innocent,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:58.240 --> 00:05:02.640
or allowing innocent deaths to occur. But&nbsp;
Carnage's bloodlust was indiscriminate, and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:02.640 --> 00:05:07.040
when Spider-Man asked for Venom's help in stopping&nbsp;
the killing spree, Venom agreed. It was the first&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:07.040 --> 00:05:11.280
time they would team up to take down Venom's&nbsp;
crimson offspring, but certainly not the last.

00:05:12.160 --> 00:05:15.440
After dealing with Carnage together,&nbsp;
Spider-Man and Venom eventually worked&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:15.440 --> 00:05:18.480
out a truce. That story involved&nbsp;
both Peter's long-lost parents,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:18.480 --> 00:05:23.120
recently returned and soon to be revealed as&nbsp;
imposters, and Eddie Brock's ex-wife, Anne Weying.

00:05:23.120 --> 00:05:28.560
"Amazing Spider-Man" #375 was billed as "the&nbsp;
final confrontation," as Spider-Man battled&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:28.560 --> 00:05:32.480
Venom in an abandoned theme park, determined&nbsp;
to stop him for good. Anne, who had helped&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:32.480 --> 00:05:36.640
Spider-Man locate her former husband, arrived on&nbsp;
the scene to try and help, but ended up nearly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:36.640 --> 00:05:41.280
being crushed by a falling ferris wheel. Venom and&nbsp;
Spider-Man were forced to join forces to save her,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:41.280 --> 00:05:45.680
and afterward, Anne helped Venom realize that&nbsp;
Spider-Man regularly saves innocent lives.

00:05:45.680 --> 00:05:48.320
This revelation finally led&nbsp;
to a truce between the two,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:48.320 --> 00:05:52.160
with Venom swinging away to San Francisco&nbsp;
and into his own limited series, "Venom:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:52.160 --> 00:05:56.240
Lethal Protector." It was actually Spider-Man&nbsp;
who ended up breaking the truce in that series&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:56.240 --> 00:06:00.160
when he went hunting for the escaped Venom, but&nbsp;
by the end, the two were working together again,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:00.160 --> 00:06:04.480
with Venom having completed his transformation&nbsp;
into a hero… or at least an anti-hero.

00:06:05.280 --> 00:06:10.240
Venom spent a solid decade from the mid-90's to&nbsp;
the mid-2000s hanging around the Marvel Universe&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:10.240 --> 00:06:14.480
as a popular anti-hero, starring in numerous&nbsp;
limited series and finally getting his first&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:14.480 --> 00:06:18.640
ongoing title in 2003. Over this period,&nbsp;
he had more adventures with Anne Weying,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:18.640 --> 00:06:22.560
who spent some time as She-Venom, and attempted&nbsp;
to train (and then, when that went south,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:22.560 --> 00:06:27.040
fight to the death) a new symbiote and host&nbsp;
entity called Toxin -- among other adventures.

00:06:27.040 --> 00:06:31.280
It was eventually revealed that the Venom symbiote&nbsp;
was the only thing keeping the cancer inside Eddie&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:31.280 --> 00:06:35.600
from killing him. Eddie, meanwhile also started&nbsp;
to question whether being bonded to the symbiote&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:35.600 --> 00:06:40.240
was influencing him towards violence, a theory&nbsp;
seemingly confirmed by his eventual slide back&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:40.240 --> 00:06:44.240
into villainy, and specifically a hatred&nbsp;
for Spider-Man. The truce between the two&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:44.240 --> 00:06:48.720
officially ended when Anne commited suicide,&nbsp;
and Venom believed Spider-Man was the cause.

00:06:48.720 --> 00:06:51.760
In 2004, the symbiote went&nbsp;
full villain once again,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:51.760 --> 00:06:56.080
though Eddie Brock did not. Having experienced&nbsp;
a religious re-awakening after watching "The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:56.080 --> 00:06:58.880
Passion of the Christ," Brock&nbsp;
finally gave up being Venom,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:58.880 --> 00:07:03.040
selling the symbiote at a supervillain auction.&nbsp;
The symbiote first possessed the son of the mob&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:03.040 --> 00:07:08.160
boss who bought him before finding a more suitable&nbsp;
host in Mac Gargan, aka the Scorpion, and remained&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:08.160 --> 00:07:12.640
an antagonist of Spider-Man and various other&nbsp;
Marvel heroes for the remainder of the 2000s.

00:07:13.360 --> 00:07:19.200
From 2011 to 2017, Venom's host was a very&nbsp;
different Spider-Man character — Flash Thompson,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:19.200 --> 00:07:23.200
former Spider-Man admirer and Peter Parker&nbsp;
bully, who lost his legs while serving in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:23.200 --> 00:07:27.360
the military. When the government decided to put&nbsp;
the Venom symbiote to use, it gave it to Flash,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:27.360 --> 00:07:31.040
allowing him to walk again and transforming&nbsp;
him into the heroic Agent Venom.

00:07:31.040 --> 00:07:34.240
The symbiote wasn't bonded to Flash&nbsp;
at first — he was only allowed to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:34.240 --> 00:07:38.800
use it for 48 hours at a time — and their&nbsp;
relationship was an openly antagonistic one,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:38.800 --> 00:07:43.520
with the symbiote taking any opportunity to seize&nbsp;
control and perform monstrous acts of violence.

00:07:43.520 --> 00:07:47.760
Most of Agent Venom's story doesn't directly&nbsp;
involve Spider-Man, but their paths crossed in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:47.760 --> 00:07:51.600
unusual fashion in the pages of "Superior&nbsp;
Spider-Man." The premise of this title&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:51.600 --> 00:07:56.000
involved a mind swap between Peter Parker&nbsp;
and his longtime nemesis Otto Octavius,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:56.000 --> 00:08:00.960
aka Doctor Octopus, who continued to fight&nbsp;
crime as Spider-Man while in his rival's body.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:00.960 --> 00:08:05.440
As Spider-Man, Octavius forcibly extracted&nbsp;
the symbiote from Flash and became host to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:05.440 --> 00:08:10.560
it himself — calling himself the Superior Venom.&nbsp;
In a fascinating reversal, however, the symbiote&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:10.560 --> 00:08:14.960
sensed something wrong with its old flame. While&nbsp;
it briefly tasted freedom by taking full control&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:14.960 --> 00:08:20.000
of Spider-Man's body, it was expelled by a remnant&nbsp;
of Peter's mind and returned willingly to Flash.

00:08:20.880 --> 00:08:25.440
Things didn't get any less weird for Agent Venom&nbsp;
after dealing with the Superior Spider-Man — in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:25.440 --> 00:08:29.840
fact, he ended up going to space and joining the&nbsp;
Guardians of the Galaxy. One of his adventures&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:29.840 --> 00:08:34.080
while on the team finally gave an origin story,&nbsp;
and even a home planet, to the symbiotes.

00:08:34.080 --> 00:08:39.200
This story introduced Klyntar, home of the&nbsp;
symbiote hive. Originally a species of conquerors,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:39.200 --> 00:08:43.440
the Klyntar had repented of their ancient evil&nbsp;
ways, seeking instead to become a force for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:43.440 --> 00:08:47.760
good. They formed the Agents of the Cosmos,&nbsp;
an organization of symbiotes bound to worthy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:47.760 --> 00:08:52.080
hosts who were dedicated to fostering peace and&nbsp;
justice throughout the universe. Some symbiotes,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:52.080 --> 00:08:56.080
however, had been corrupted by their hosts,&nbsp;
and the Venom symbiote was one of these.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:56.080 --> 00:08:59.120
Upon its arrival back home, the&nbsp;
Klyntar were able to cleanse it,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:59.120 --> 00:09:04.080
a process that included a near-total memory wipe&nbsp;
of its previous hosts. As a result, when Agent&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:04.080 --> 00:09:08.800
Venom returned to Earth and once again encountered&nbsp;
Spider-Man, it had no memory of him. The symbiote&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:08.800 --> 00:09:12.720
even apologized to Spider-Man and expressed&nbsp;
a desire to one day earn his forgiveness.

00:09:13.600 --> 00:09:17.920
If the Klyntar memory wipe set the stage for&nbsp;
a reconciliation between Venom and Spider-Man,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:17.920 --> 00:09:22.480
the events of 2018 and 2019 brought their&nbsp;
relationship full circle. By that point,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:22.480 --> 00:09:25.920
the Venom symbiote had been separated&nbsp;
from Flash Thompson, and after a brief&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:25.920 --> 00:09:30.000
fling with an ex-soldier named Lee Price,&nbsp;
it became bonded to Eddie Brock once again,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:30.000 --> 00:09:33.120
and they were once more the star&nbsp;
of a "Venom" ongoing series.

00:09:33.120 --> 00:09:35.680
"It is happening again."

00:09:35.680 --> 00:09:40.240
When Carnage bonded with legendary Spider-Man&nbsp;
nemesis Norman Osborn to become the Red Goblin,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:40.240 --> 00:09:44.880
Spider-Man and Venom, as usual, teamed up to&nbsp;
oppose him. In order to defeat Red Goblin, Brock&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:44.880 --> 00:09:49.200
willingly gave up the symbiote to Spider-Man,&nbsp;
who donned it again in "Amazing Spider-Man"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:49.200 --> 00:09:54.160
#800. After the Red Goblin's defeat, the symbiote&nbsp;
was transferred peacefully back to Brock. It was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:54.160 --> 00:09:57.760
a sequence of events that demonstrated&nbsp;
how far the two characters had come.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:57.760 --> 00:10:02.560
And as if to reinforce it, during the 2019&nbsp;
event "Absolute Carnage," the symbiote itself&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:02.560 --> 00:10:07.200
convinced Brock to join forces with Spider-Man&nbsp;
yet again — a story that ended with Eddie Brock,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:07.200 --> 00:10:12.000
who had sworn to kill Spider-Man on numerous&nbsp;
occasions, actually giving his old enemy a hug.

